# opencode-create-image Plugin Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Build an opencode plugin (npm package `opencode-create-image`) that registers a `create_image` tool calling any OpenAI-compatible `/images/generations` API, saving images to disk, plus an optional companion skill.

**Architecture:** ESM plugin module exporting a `Plugin` function. `src/index.ts` registers the `create_image` tool via `tool()`; `src/config.ts` resolves settings (plugin options -> env -> defaults); `src/image.ts` calls the API with `fetch`, writes the file, and returns a `ToolResult` with a file attachment. Repo ships on GitHub; package publishes to npm manually; install = `opencode plugin opencode-create-image`.

**Tech Stack:** TypeScript, tsup, vitest, `@opencode-ai/plugin` (dependency), global `fetch`, `node:fs/promises`. Build tool: Bun.

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-14-create-image-plugin-design.md`

## Global Constraints

- Package name exactly `opencode-create-image`, `"type": "module"`, `main`/`exports` point to `./dist/index.js`.
- `@opencode-ai/plugin` pinned `^1.18.18` as a runtime dependency.
- API default base URL `https://api.openai.com/v1`; default model `gpt-image-1`; default size `1024x1024`; default quality `auto`; default output dir `images`.
- Config precedence: tool arg -> plugin option -> env var (`OPENAI_API_KEY`/`OPENAI_KEY`, `OPENAI_BASE_URL`, `OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL`) -> default.
- No `release.yml`, no AGENTS.md, no system-prompt injection, no `n` tool arg.

